cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the archived release in your work, please cite
  the versioned Zenodo archive referenced below.
title: >-
  Hybrid Unimodular Hill and Logistic Map XOR Scheme for Binary Files
  (experimental proof of concept)
type: software
authors:
  - name: Dwi Wijonarko
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/dwi-wijonarko-unej/hybrid-uhc-logistic-binary-files
url: https://github.com/dwi-wijonarko-unej/hybrid-uhc-logistic-binary-files
abstract: >-
  Experimental evaluation framework for a hybrid file cipher that combines a
  unimodular 16 x 16 Hill transform over Z/256Z on 256-byte blocks with a
  byte-wise XOR against a logistic-map keystream. Includes exact modular
  matrix inversion (Gauss-Jordan with unit pivots and the extended
  Euclidean algorithm), a reproducible benchmark and statistics pipeline,
  and a revised real-format DOCX/PDF/JPEG benchmark with deterministic
  seeded test data. This is not modern authenticated encryption; it is a
  proof of concept for evaluating reversibility, byte statistics, and
  runtime only.
keywords:
  - hill cipher
  - unimodular matrix
  - logistic map
  - keystream
  - reproducibility
  - proof of concept
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
